Step 2: The final "fault sweeps" part of gpu_test.sh initially failed to run due to a stray "cd /" statement. I edited this out before committing the file to the Git repository. When it did run, that part took a couple of hours rather than 5 minutes you anticipated for this entire step. But it did complete successfully.
Step 3: k2 was the fastest, with k4 a close second, almost twice as fast as fused.
Step 4: The interim residues at 1M intervals all matched the ones during the CPU run in the last round, and irreducibillity is confirmed. I have now included that CPU run (from November 20, 2026) here for comparison as irred_cpu_12338357.log even though it belongs to an earlier round.


